        <parameter>
            <valueName>layer:SOREM:1.0:Broadcast_Text</valueName>
            <value>At 4:56 p.m. Eastern Daylight Time Thursday, Environment Canada has issued a marine tornado warning for Lower Great Lakes. Extra care and attention should be exercised in the following marine areas: Lake Erie. Environment Canada meteorologists are tracking severe thunderstorms that are possibly producing tornadoes. Damaging winds, large hail and locally intense rainfall are possible. Tornadoes are often wrapped in rain and may not be visible. Take cover immediately if threatening weather approaches.</value>
